      "content": "thanks. one thing i'm curious about for the article—whenever i read about this, the scientific arguments always seem so much more concrete because they're based on math and biology, while the civil liberties side often feels like it's just based on abstract philosophy or \"feelings\" about freedom. do you think there's a way to reconcile the two, or is one side just fundamentally more \"correct\" when it comes to policy making?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
